      "comparisonSentence": "Unlike raw vegetables, these vegetable stir-fries and rice staples introduce cooking oils and refined starches that require portion moderation.",
      "message": "Tumis (stir-fried) greens provide essential vitamins and minerals, but they are typically prepared with added cooking oil and savory seasonings, increasing total fat and sodium. Standard white rice or Nasi Uduk adds a higher glycemic load, so portion control is important for metabolic regulation.",
      "orderingTip": "Request less oil ('sedikit minyak') when ordering vegetable stir-fries, and opt for plain white rice over Nasi Uduk to keep glycemic impact moderate."
