      "verdict": {
        "label": "Severe Metabolic & Cardiovascular Load",
        "level": "alert"
      },
      "comparisonSentence": "Pencok dishes, fried organ meats, and fried cabbage carry an excessive cardiovascular risk due to concentrated trans/saturated fats and high sodium.",
      "message": "Deep-fried organ meats (Sate Usus, Sate Kulit), fried cabbage (Kol Goreng), and nut-based pencok preparations absorb large amounts of cooking oil during high-heat frying. This creates a dense concentration of inflammatory fats and sodium that places heavy stress on cardiovascular and renal pathways.",
      "orderingTip": "Strictly avoid fried cabbage and deep-fried organ skewers; substitute them with fresh cucumber or raw greens."
